  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The paper is a high-level conceptual intervention and agenda-setting piece rather than an empirical study presenting new datasets or quantitative measurements.",
      "what": "This paper outlines a conceptual framework for analyzing the spatial and temporal dimensions of inequalities, serving as the introductory theme for the RGS-IBG 2026 Annual Conference. It reviews the methodological techniques geographers use to investigate structural and institutional injustices and examines how professional and academic practices can actively resist these disparities.",
      "why": "It establishes a disciplinary agenda that connects theoretical critiques of inequality directly to institutional reform and professional practices, shifting the focus from merely documenting spatial disparities to actively constructing just places."
